42. Navigator.pop()

This is the most important line on the second screen:

Navigator.pop(context);

pop() means:

Remove the current screen from the navigation stack.

Remember our stack:

SecondScreen   ← current
HomeScreen

After:

Navigator.pop(context);

the stack becomes:

HomeScreen     ← current

So the user returns to HomeScreen.

Complete Flow

The entire application works like this:

              Application starts
                     │
                     ▼
                  main()
                     │
                     ▼
                runApp()
                     │
                     ▼
                  MyApp
                     │
                     ▼
               MaterialApp
                     │
                     ▼
                HomeScreen
                     │
             Press button
                     │
                     ▼
            Navigator.push()
                     │
                     ▼
              SecondScreen
                     │
             Press Go Back
                     │
                     ▼
            Navigator.pop()
                     │
                     ▼
                HomeScreen
The two most important concepts
push() = Go forward
Navigator.push(
  context,
  MaterialPageRoute(
    builder: (context) => const SecondScreen(),
  ),
);

Think:

Push = Open a new page

pop() = Go backward
Navigator.pop(context);

Think:

Pop = Close the current page

A useful way to remember it is:

Navigator Stack

        ┌───────────────┐
        │ SecondScreen  │ ← push adds this
        ├───────────────┤
        │ HomeScreen    │
        └───────────────┘

                 ↓ pop

        ┌───────────────┐
        │ HomeScreen    │ ← back here
        └───────────────┘